logicgates.direction.east = east (+X)
logicgates.direction.south = south (+Z)
logicgates.direction.west = west (-X)
logicgates.input.absent = empty (ignored)
logicgates.input.off = connected, signal 0
logicgates.input.on = connected, signal 1
logicgates.input.unavailable = section unavailable (not empty)
logicgates.input.incompatible = incompatible face (not connected)
logicgates.reason.logic = The output follows the connected inputs and the gate rule. External power at the output does not change this indicator.
logicgates.reason.no_inputs = No inputs are connected: output is 0, including inverting gates.
logicgates.reason.section_unavailable = An input section is unavailable: output is held at 0 until it returns.
logicgates.reason.indeterminate_feedback = Feedback has no determined value under this combinational policy: output is held at 0. This is not a memory or clock.
logicgates.help.intro = A/B are the sides, C is the rear and the arrow is the only output. NOT only uses C. Connections are horizontal.
logicgates.help.optional = Empty inputs are ignored; connected signal 0 counts. No inputs: output 0 for every gate. Each face counts separately, even on the same cable network.
logicgates.help.feedback = Indicator = gate result, not external output power. Unavailable sections or undetermined feedback hold the output at 0. Use /logicinspect x y z to see why.
logicgates.help.usage = Example: /logichelp --gate=XOR --inputs=3. /logicinspect x y z; console: also specify --world=<name>.
logicgates.help.invalidGate = Choose AND, OR, NOT, NAND, NOR, XOR or XNOR.
logicgates.help.invalidInputs = Choose 1, 2 or 3 connected inputs. NOT accepts only 1.
logicgates.help.table = {gate}: truth table with {inputs} connected; other inputs are empty.
logicgates.help.row = {inputs} -> {output}

